{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuiqEsNKT1wNPxyW2CDj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not directly. The Agents SDK's `this.schedule()` (along with `getSchedules()` and `cancelSchedule()`) is a method on the `Agent` class. It's built on top of the Durable Object alarms API and stores its schedule queue in the Agent's SQLite storage, so a class that only extends `DurableObject` doesn't have it.\n\nYou have two options:\n\n- **Extend `Agent`.** An `Agent` is itself a Durable Object, so you lose nothing, and you can ignore the WebSocket and state features you don't need.\n- **Use alarms directly.** Call `this.ctx.storage.setAlarm()` and implement `alarm()` yourself. Each Durable Object gets only one alarm at a time, so for multiple or cron-style schedules you'd keep your own queue in storage and always set the alarm to the earliest due time. That's essentially what the SDK does for you.\n\nI answered this from memory and didn't check the current docs. If a recent SDK release added a standalone scheduling helper, it would be listed in the Cloudflare Agents changelog."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5818,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5818},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"168908fc-ac4b-49a4-9b54-c8000cd5afd1","uuid":"280850ae-d515-4aa6-9172-018e87f1cc2d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:15:00.311Z","request_id":"req_011CfuiqEeToqaKRQAPq3oWk"}
